\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Positive marginals and their observable domains}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{In the specific cellular sign-link marginal of
\ref{fdip-00XZ}, the geometric reflection fixes each of the
#{4} connections individually and the assigned masses are
positive. Its diagonal integrand is then #{|f(U)|^2} for
every observable on those connections. Positivity there holds
on the whole function algebra. In \ref{fdip-019O} reflection
instead exchanges distinct connections carrying opposite
values of #{q}.}

\p{\ref{fdip-00PZ} concerns the massive scalar measure with
positive reflection-invariant weights. Its positive domain
consists of scalar-field observables. For fermionic
observables the Grassmann factors have their own reflected
order. A fermionic transfer theorem needs the spin projectors,
adjoint, boundary conditions, gauge constraint and observable
correspondence specified in \ref{fdip-00JB}. These are
additional inputs to a transfer construction.}
